{
  "_comment": "fetch_many(urls, options): the JSON body sent to POST /v1/fetch (\"body\" cases) and what a success body becomes (\"responses\" cases). Options are named as the SDK arguments (urls, text, max_chars, offset, summary, output_schema, highlights, highlights_query, highlights_max_chars, links, images, subpages, subpages_target, max_age, page_timeout, session_id, end_user_id); each SDK maps them to its own spelling. Body rules: urls are sent as given (a lone string is wrapped in a list); content.text is true unless text is false, or {max_chars, offset} with the ones set; summary is {instructions} plus output_schema when given, and output_schema alone is sent as {output_schema} for the API to reject; highlights is true, or {query, max_chars} with the ones set, sent when highlights is true or either detail is set; links and images are sent as given numbers; subpages is {max, target} with the ones set, sent when subpages or subpages_target is set (target as given: a string or a list), and subpages_target alone is sent as {target} for the API to reject; max_age, page_timeout (as \"timeout\"), session_id and end_user_id are sent as given, an empty string meaning unset. `sent` is the whole body, compared as JSON. Response rules: results and warnings are lists of objects (anything else is []), non-object entries skipped. A result's url is the string sent or \"\"; title, published_at, image, favicon and text are a non-blank string or null; next_offset an integer from 0 to 2^53 - 1 or null (total_chars is not read); summary is a non-blank string, an object, or null; highlights the strings in the list; links [{url, text}] and images [{url, alt}] with url \"\" and text/alt null for anything else; subpages the result objects in the list, read by these same rules ([] otherwise). A result's error is null unless it is an object; then its code and message are strings (\"\" otherwise), retryable a boolean (false otherwise), http_status an integer or null. A warning's code, path and message are strings (\"\" otherwise). request_id is the body's non-blank string, else the trimmed X-Request-Id header, else null; latency_ms an integer from 0 or null; session_id a non-blank string or null. `skip` names an SDK whose types cannot express the case, with why. Stream cases (fetch_many_stream, Accept: application/x-ndjson): the reply is the NDJSON text in `chunks`, delivered chunk by chunk, so a line can be split across chunks. Each non-blank line is a JSON object (a trailing \\r is ignored). A line without done: true is an item: its index (an integer from 0, else the item is skipped) and its other fields read as a result by the rules above. The line with done: true ends the stream: its request_id (else the trimmed X-Request-Id header), latency_ms, session_id and warnings read as above, and usage is the object as sent or null. If that line has an error object, the stream raises the API error with its code, message and retryable after yielding every item before it. A stream that ends without a done line, or a line that is not a JSON object, raises the connection error (kind \\\"connection\\\") or the API error (kind \\\"api\\\").",
  "body": [
    {"name": "one url, no options", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}}},
    {"name": "several urls in order", "urls": ["https://a.example/", "https://b.example/x", "https://a.example/"], "options": {}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://a.example/", "https://b.example/x", "https://a.example/"], "content": {"text": true}}},
    {"name": "a lone url string is wrapped", "urls": "https://example.com/", "options": {}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}}, "skip": {"go": "FetchMany takes a []string"}},
    {"name": "text limits", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"max_chars": 20000, "offset": 20000}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": {"max_chars": 20000, "offset": 20000}}}},
    {"name": "max_chars alone", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"max_chars": 500}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": {"max_chars": 500}}}},
    {"name": "text off with a summary", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"text": false, "summary": "List the prices"}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"summary": {"instructions": "List the prices"}}}},
    {"name": "text and a summary together", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"summary": "List the prices"}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true, "summary": {"instructions": "List the prices"}}}},
    {"name": "a summary with an output schema", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"text": false, "summary": "Card fees", "output_schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pct": {"type": "number"}}}}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"summary": {"instructions": "Card fees", "output_schema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pct": {"type": "number"}}}}}}},
    {"name": "an output schema alone is sent for the API to reject", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"text": false, "output_schema": {"type": "object"}}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"summary": {"output_schema": {"type": "object"}}}}},
    {"name": "highlights with defaults", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"text": false, "highlights": true}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"highlights": true}}},
    {"name": "highlights with a query and a budget", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"text": false, "highlights_query": "pricing", "highlights_max_chars": 3000}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"highlights": {"query": "pricing", "max_chars": 3000}}}},
    {"name": "links and images", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"links": 50, "images": 5}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true, "links": 50, "images": 5}}},
    {"name": "freshness and timeout", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"max_age": "1d", "page_timeout": "15s"}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "max_age": "1d", "timeout": "15s"}},
    {"name": "always live", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"max_age": "0s"}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "max_age": "0s"}},
    {"name": "session and end user", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"session_id": "chat-42", "end_user_id": "user_7"}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "session_id": "chat-42", "end_user_id": "user_7"}},
    {"name": "empty strings are unset", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"summary": "", "highlights_query": "", "max_age": "", "page_timeout": "", "session_id": "", "end_user_id": ""}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}}},
    {"name": "zero links is sent", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"links": 0}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true, "links": 0}}, "skip": {"go": "FetchManyOptions.Links is an int whose zero means unset"}},
    {"name": "every option", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"max_chars": 1000, "offset": 10, "summary": "S", "output_schema": {"type": "object"}, "highlights_query": "q", "highlights_max_chars": 200, "links": 3, "images": 2, "max_age": "2h", "page_timeout": "30s", "session_id": "s", "end_user_id": "u"}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": {"max_chars": 1000, "offset": 10}, "summary": {"instructions": "S", "output_schema": {"type": "object"}}, "highlights": {"query": "q", "max_chars": 200}, "links": 3, "images": 2}, "max_age": "2h", "timeout": "30s", "session_id": "s", "end_user_id": "u"}},
    {"name": "subpages with a count", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"subpages": 5}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "subpages": {"max": 5}}},
    {"name": "subpages with target words", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"subpages": 3, "subpages_target": ["pricing", "docs"]}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "subpages": {"max": 3, "target": ["pricing", "docs"]}}},
    {"name": "subpages with one target word", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"subpages": 3, "subpages_target": "pricing"}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "subpages": {"max": 3, "target": "pricing"}}, "skip": {"go": "SubpagesTarget is a []string"}},
    {"name": "subpages target alone is sent for the API to reject", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"subpages_target": ["pricing"]}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "subpages": {"target": ["pricing"]}}},
    {"name": "stored copies only", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"cache_only": true}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "cache_only": true}},
    {"name": "stored copies only, no older than a day", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"cache_only": true, "max_age": "1d"}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "max_age": "1d", "cache_only": true}},
    {"name": "subpages up to 100", "urls": ["https://example.com/"], "options": {"subpages": 100}, "sent": {"urls": ["https://example.com/"], "content": {"text": true}, "subpages": {"max": 100}}}
